    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d92">

                <pb facs="0193" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.6363/9</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 10.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 596</seg></opener>
                <p>Sir: Referring to my telegram No. 862, of October 27, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >5</hi>] p.m.,<anchor n="42" xml:id="d92-f1"/> in reference to the
                    representatives of the Standard Oil Company in Jerusalem, and their desire to
                    continue geological examinations, I have the honor to transmit herewith copies
                    of the full text of the Note referred to, together with a copy of my Note to the
                    Foreign Office, No. 189 of September 15.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Post
                            Wheeler</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>




                <xi:include href="d92-a1.xml" xpointer="d92-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d92-a2.xml" xpointer="d92-a2"/>
            </div>
